# RBWS FVI Extractor — Agent Guide

You are working on **rbws-fvi-extractor**: recreate a manually prepared **RBWS Excel** from Jimcel/ExxonMobil (or SEPLAT) **Fire Water / FVI inspection PDFs**.

## Goal (source of truth)

- **Input:** FVI PDF (image-only or native-text), same family as `UBIT-GP_FVI_FWS_*.pdf`, `YOHO-YA_FVI_FWS_*.pdf`
- **Output:** Excel matching gold layout (e.g. sheet `UBIT-GP` / facility name), **not** a generic OCR dump
- **Gold Excel** (when available) defines row rules — reverse-engineer from it, don’t invent columns

## Default approach: local only (no API)

**Preferred engine: `--engine ocr` (default).** No LLM / OpenAI / Gemini / NVIDIA required.

Pipeline:

1. Render PDF pages → PNG (`PdfRenderer`)
2. Prefer **native PDF text** if rich enough; else **Tesseract OCR**
3. Parse with deterministic rules (`ocr/jimcel_native.py` for clean Jimcel tables; `ocr/parsers.py` OCR heuristics fallback)
4. Apply gold **finding/row rules** (`pipeline/detect_findings.py`, `configs/rbws_columns.yaml`)
5. Crop Photos/ISO from page renders (`ocr/crop.py`) and embed in Excel (`excel/writer.py`)

Optional LLM path exists (`--engine llm`) but is **not** the default and was abandoned for quota/reliability; keep it secondary.

## Excel schema (header row 2, data from row 3, cols B–Q)

| Col | Header | Category | Rule |
|-----|--------|----------|------|
| B | S/N | B | Sequential |
| C | Insp Date | A | From metadata page; stamp all rows |
| D | Line # | A | See asset rules below |
| E | Line Pressure (Psi) | C | **Always blank** |
| F | Line Description | A | From table / Equipment ID |
| G | Anomaly Description | A | From captions/table/summary |
| H | P&ID No | A | Blank for cylinders & pump/caisson |
| I–M | POF, Consq, Driver, Risk, IRU | C | **Always blank** |
| N | Photos | A | Cropped embedded image |
| O | ISO | A | Sketch crop when applicable |
| P–Q | Quest Recommendations, Remarks | C | **Always blank** (automation scope) |

Category C = engineering judgment — leave blank unless user explicitly asks otherwise.

## Report structure (Jimcel FVI template)

Typical sections:

- Cover / metadata TOC (facility, report #, WO, inspection date, cover P&IDs)
- **§1** Summary of findings (bullets + Photo # ranges)
- **§2** Visual inspection observation tables (piping, hose, monitor, diesel, cylinders)
- **§3** Equipment anomaly photographic details (`Equipment ID` + Photo captions); may include ISO sketch (“DRAWING NOT TO SCALE”)
- **§4** Lines found on P&ID with no line number (untagged), when present
- Some sections marked **NOT APPLICABLE** → skip (no rows)

**Note:** Cover/TOC P&IDs often differ from **row-level** P&IDs in §2 tables. Prefer table/row P&ID for findings.

## Gold row-creation rules (critical)

### Fire protection cylinders
- **One §3 `Equipment ID` block = one Excel row** (include good-condition cylinders)
- Line # = `Fire protection cylinder`
- Line Description = Equipment ID text
- P&ID = blank
- Anomaly from Photo captions; keep Photo # refs in text when useful
- ISO = none

### Fire water pump & caisson
- **Aggregate all pump/caisson evidence into ONE row**
- Line # = `Fire water pump & caisson`
- Line Description = blank; P&ID = blank
- If section is NOT APPLICABLE → **no row**

### Tagged piping (§2.3)
- One table row = one Excel row
- **Exclude** “Visually in good condition” (and similar)
- Line # = tagged line (e.g. `WF-010-8"-40-FAA-4` or `WF-9024-2"-CBR-0`)
- Keep P&ID from table
- Photos + ISO when sketch pages match line number

### Hose reel / monitor / diesel (§2.4–2.6)
- Keep anomaly rows (usually “No tag found” for hose/monitor)
- Diesel: Line # = equipment tag (e.g. `GP-G-03`); synthesize description if needed
- Skip entire asset class if NOT APPLICABLE

### Untagged lines (§4)
- Like piping: exclude good-condition rows
- Often different P&ID series (e.g. `…0050801`)

### Photos / ISO images
- Map finding `Photo #` refs → detail pages (§3+), **not** summary pages that only cite photo numbers
- Crop photo grid region; if page has ISO sketch below photos, crop upper = Photos, lower = ISO
- Stitch multiple photo pages vertically if needed
- Cylinders / pump / diesel typically **no ISO**

