## How to run (local)

```bash
cd /Users/shivendrajaiswal/Developer/rbws-fvi-extractor
source .venv/bin/activate
PYTHONPATH=src python -m rbws_extractor.main \
  --engine ocr \
  --pdf /path/to/REPORT.pdf \
  --output outputs/REPORT_RBWS.xlsx \
  --work-dir outputs/report_run
```

Reuse existing page PNGs: `--reuse-pages outputs/.../pages`  
Skip images: `--skip-images`

## When given a new PDF

1. Inspect page count + native text vs image-only
2. Read metadata + §1–§2 tables + sample §3 Equipment ID pages
3. Prefer `jimcel_native` if text is clean; else OCR path
4. Honor NOT APPLICABLE sections
5. Generalize line-number regexes (FAA-*, CBR-*, curly quotes `’`)
6. Produce Excel with Photos/ISO; compare finding count/types to §1 summary totals
7. Do **not** call external LLMs unless user explicitly requests `--engine llm`

## Non-goals

- Filling POF / recommendations / risk (judgment)
- Generic full-document OCR dump without RBWS row semantics
- Treating cover P&ID list as per-row P&ID
